<title>USA: Jefferson-Pilot 1998 estimate raised.</title>
<headline>Jefferson-Pilot 1998 estimate raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers analyst Ed Spehar raised his estimate for Jefferson-Pilot Corp's 1998 operating earnings to $4.75 a share from $4.45, saying the acquisition of Chubb Corp's life insurance business will serve as a catalyst for outperformance.</p>
<p>Spehar, in a report, said he raised his 12-month price target to $75 a share from $65.</p>
<p>&quot;In general, given that Chubb's life insurance business has a solid balance sheet and that Jefferson-Pilot is acquiring it at book value, we believe that positive surprises are more likely than negative ones,&quot; Spehar wrote.</p>
<p>On Monday, Jefferson-Pilot announced a definitive agreement to buy Chubb's life insurance business for $875 million in cash.</p>
<p>Jefferson-Pilot shares rose 3/8 to 59-7/8 in early afternoon trading.</p>
